{"total_count":9,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commits/7778d96d4291e55e332f2124bda43abc5fae57e3","sha":"7778d96d4291e55e332f2124bda43abc5fae57e3","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MzY1Njk3NDkzOjc3NzhkOTZkNDI5MWU1NWUzMzJmMjEyNGJkYTQzYWJjNWZhZTU3ZTM=","html_url":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commit/7778d96d4291e55e332f2124bda43abc5fae57e3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/commits/7778d96d4291e55e332f2124bda43abc5fae57e3/comments","commit":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/commits/7778d96d4291e55e332f2124bda43abc5fae57e3","author":{"date":"2022-04-28T15:22:51.000Z","name":"Henrik Böving","email":"hargonix@gmail.com"},"committer":{"date":"2022-04-28T15:22:51.000Z","name":"Henrik Böving","email":"hargonix@gmail.com"},"message":"feat: slim check (#254)\n\nAn absolute minimal port of Lean 3's slim_check, not featuring stuff like subtypes, existential quantifiers etc. But the basic infrastructure to set all of this up and some basic instances already as well.\r\n\r\nThe `PhantomFunction` was introduced to avoid noncomputable instances since `SizeOf` is not computable but we need to store it as a field in `SampleableExt` so we work around this by defining a `PhantomFunction` which is guaranteed to be eliminated by the compiler during code generation. I do however believe that this is not the right file for it to live in?","tree":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/trees/289c6b97d8ff8c662e4cff664e031755d1f8d9cc","sha":"289c6b97d8ff8c662e4cff664e031755d1f8d9cc"},"comment_count":0},"author":{"login":"hargoniX","id":33270164,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjcwMTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33270164?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hargoniX","html_url":"https://github.com/hargoniX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hargoniX/follow